If the basic-neighbourhood enumeration is primitive recursive, then the one-step tree lookup is primitive recursive.

The leaf value is the enumeration of the payload, and the node value is the universal intersection of the two table lookups of the children; both are primitive recursive. The tag is primitive recursive, and the predicates that it equals 1 and that it equals 2 select among the leaf value, the node value, and the master index. Matching on the tag shows that this selection is the body of the lookup.
